WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.627 --> 00:00:04.004
Okay, let's go.

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:06.631
- Rock, paper, scissors!
- Rock, paper, scissors!

00:00:07.966 --> 00:00:10.427
Congratulations! You win, Jabami.

00:00:11.553 --> 00:00:12.637
What next?

00:00:13.471 --> 00:00:14.723
Let's see.

00:00:18.476 --> 00:00:21.396
Shall we go with 50 chips once more?

00:00:21.479 --> 00:00:24.399
Are you kidding me?
Didn't you get burned enough?

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.152
Interesting.

00:00:28.486 --> 00:00:30.405
I like that kind of spirit.

00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:35.535
Here we go.

00:00:36.077 --> 00:00:38.038
- Rock, paper, scissors!
- Rock, paper, scissors!

00:00:40.331 --> 00:00:41.875
Great minds do think alike.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:44.377
Here we go again.

00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:48.381
We have a...

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:49.382
- Tie!
- Tie!

00:00:57.015 --> 00:00:59.851
Yes! I win yet again!

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.687
Thanks for the 500,000.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.024
That's one million yen, total.

00:01:06.107 --> 00:01:08.526
All right, next!
Let's keep rolling, shall we?

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:11.529
Is something wrong?

00:01:12.113 --> 00:01:14.532
Don't tell me you're getting cold feet.

00:01:14.616 --> 00:01:18.620
Well, after losing one million yen,
who can blame you?

00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:23.541
No, the showdown
is just about to start.

00:01:24.125 --> 00:01:26.252
Please bet two chips this time around.

00:01:28.713 --> 00:01:33.510
It's over. 216 chips versus 24 chips.
The gap is way too huge.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.345
Her back's up against the wall.

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.514
She'll never pull off an upset
if she's freaked out.

00:01:38.973 --> 00:01:40.725
Then let's carry on.

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:43.728
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:01:43.812 --> 00:01:44.646
Scissors!

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:46.064
Scissors!

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:52.570
Oh, my, Jabami.
I see you've run out of chips.

00:01:52.654 --> 00:01:56.074
- Did she just lose 1.2 million yen?
- That was a huge gamble.

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:59.911
Mary, would you mind playing
just one more game?

00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:02.539
Don't do it, Jabami!

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:06.292
At the rate you're going,
you'll be a house pet on your first day.

00:02:06.376 --> 00:02:09.295
Of course!
How much do you want to bet?

00:02:10.004 --> 00:02:13.299
Idiot. You'll only get yourself mired
with no way out.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:18.096
Ten million yen in cash.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:26.396
Why would you walk around
with that amount of cash?

00:02:28.022 --> 00:02:29.607
Don't be ridiculous!

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:33.611
Staking ten million yen on a single
casual game of Rock-Paper-Scissors.

00:02:33.695 --> 00:02:35.113
You...

00:02:36.614 --> 00:02:37.699
You're insane!

00:02:37.782 --> 00:02:43.454
Isn't that what makes it fun? Insanity
is the essence of gambling, right?

00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:47.458
In a capitalistic society,
money and life are the same.

00:02:48.042 --> 00:02:52.463
Trusting your life to fortune,
no one in their right mind would do that.

00:02:53.047 --> 00:02:56.342
And yet, people still throng casinos
because people derive pleasure

00:02:56.426 --> 00:02:59.721
from the insanity of risking their lives.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:05.268
In that case, the more insane you are,
the more you enjoy gambling!

00:03:06.436 --> 00:03:10.148
Now, then,
let's get our gambling freak on.

